The circle $x^{2}+y^{2}=4$ is drawn below. State the coordinates of its $x$-intercepts.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.0]
\draw[<->] (-3,0)--(3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-3)--(0,3) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue] (0,0) circle (2);
\fill (0,0) circle (1.5pt);
\node[below left] at (0,0) {$O$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The circle shown is centred at the origin. Determine its equation.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.35]
\draw[<->] (-9,0)--(9,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-9)--(0,9) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue] (0,0) circle (7);
\fill (0,0) circle (3pt);
\node[below left] at (0,0) {$O$};
\fill (7,0) circle (3pt);
\node[below right] at (7,0) {$7$};
\fill (-7,0) circle (3pt);
\node[below left] at (-7,0) {$-7$};
\fill (0,7) circle (3pt);
\node[above left] at (0,7) {$7$};
\fill (0,-7) circle (3pt);
\node[below right] at (0,-7) {$-7$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
